<title>USA: Salomon, Howell offer units in Genesis MLP.</title>
<headline>Salomon, Howell offer units in Genesis MLP.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Salomon Inc said it and Howell Corp had offered 7.5 million common units of Genesis Energy MLP, which they created as an oil-gathering and pipeline company based in Houston, Texas.</p>
<p>A spokesman for Salomon said the two companies offered the units at $20.625 each.</p>
<p>He said the amount offered represented 68.18 percent of effective ownership of Genesis.</p>
<p>Salomon said in a statement the two companies had formed Genesis, a master limited partnership, to buy, own and operate the businesses of Howell and Basis Petroleum, a Salomon unit, that gather and distribute crude oil.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
